*Sessional Hymn, Tone 8, Podoben: "The Wisdom and the Word" (Премꙋ́дрости):*[^2784]  
Having learned wisdom from on high, and the grace of words from God, Thou didst shine forth unto all as gold in a furnace, and didst preach the Holy Trinity in unity, piercing the deceit of the love of silver with thy words;
...therefore also, having rebuked the empress with zeal, thou didst put to shame the alien wisdom of Arius, O John Chrysostom: entreat Christ God to grant remission of transgressions unto those who celebrate with love thy holy memory. *(Twice)*
